# Line endings: LF everywhere on checkout, on every OS.
#
# Without this, Windows runners check out with core.autocrlf=true
# and every text file becomes CRLF, which breaks two CI jobs:
# - golden rebuild check: the SHA-256 of examples/hello.py and
#   examples/showcase.py is compared against hardcoded v0 hashes,
#   and CRLF changes the hash (ubuntu/macOS pass, Windows fails).
# - standalone binary: bash chokes on the CRLF line endings of
#   scripts/build-binary.sh, so the build step fails in seconds.
# `text=auto` lets git tell text from binary, so no binary file
# is ever converted; only text files are normalized to LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
